      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Unpredictable sensor glitches in deep-sea deployments often stem from electrical noise caused by short bursts of high-current power consumption or radio frequency interference from the ship or payload. Pressure spikes or micro-vibrations during transient maneuvers can also momentarily saturate analog-to-digital converters or disrupt sensor interfaces. To troubleshoot, review the raw voltage streams before data logging and check for electromagnetic shielding failures or ground loop issues specific to that AUV segment.",
      "source": "target",
